==========================================================================
C/D. EIGENSEQUENCES, Phi_6, AND THE LAPLACIAN SPECTRUM
==========================================================================
   mu(x) = 2 - x - 1/x ;  eigen-condition x^2 + (mu-2)x + 1 = 0 (norm +1)
     mu=0: x = [1]   x=1 (double): geometric h, T(h)=1
     mu=1: x = [1/2 - sqrt(3)*I/2, 1/2 + sqrt(3)*I/2]   Phi_6(x)=x^2-x+1: primitive 6th roots -> period 6
     mu=4: x = [-1]   x=-1: pure alternation
   mu=1 polynomial IS the 6th cyclotomic polynomial: True
   on |x|=1: mu = 4 sin^2(theta/2) in [0,4]  (discrete Laplacian symbol)
     theta=pi/6   mu = 0.267949
     theta=pi/3   mu = 1.000000   <- NEUTRAL
     theta=pi/2   mu = 2.000000
     theta=2pi/3  mu = 3.000000
     theta=pi     mu = 4.000000
  VERDICT C/D: OK

==========================================================================
E. METALLIC SIMSON EIGENVALUE = DISCRIMINANT n^2+4
==========================================================================
   lambda^2 + lambda^-2 = n**2 + 2   (= n^2+2)
   Simson mode x = -lambda^-2  ->  mu = n**2 + 4   (= n^2+4 = disc)
     n=1 GOLDEN : mu = 5   <- 5 = disc(phi)
     n=2 silver : mu = 8
     n=3 BRONZE : mu = 13   <- the sqrt13 of THM-3010
     n=4 copper : mu = 20

   numeric growth rate of |log T^m| at a mid index (should tend to n^2+4):
     n=1: ratios ['5.0000', '5.0000', '5.0000', '5.0000', '5.0000']  -> predicted 5  OK
     n=2: ratios ['8.0000', '8.2500', '8.0455', '7.9944', '8.0005']  -> predicted 8  OK
  VERDICT E: OK

